A||||1||SCCA FIERO||Does  your 4 speed seem like it needs a few more inches of travel for the pedal?
Z||000000||SCCA FIERO||05-15-99||11:02 PM||||My 4 speed seemed like i needed to have alot more pedal travel to fully engage the clutch. After several bleeding procedures i started to look at the system. I noticed that the slave cylinder is mounted in the slave cylinder bracket on the outside of the bracket. I took the slave bracket off then took the slave out of the bracket. The bolts that hold the slave to the bracket are like wheel studs and press in. I knocked the bolts out and put them in the opposite way so the slave is mounted closer to the tranny. I put it all together and it's a night and day differance. I used to lift the clutch just a small amount and the car would start to move. Now i have some pedal travel before the car starts to move.
Z||000001||Patrick||05-16-99||12:24 AM||||<br>Have I got a thread for you to read!<p><b>Clutch Info uncovered...</b><p>Put a pot of coffee on and enjoy.<p> 
